    exp_07 round 9: the calibration gate validates every registered metric
    
    Round-8 blocker 2: metric_names required all five columns, but only EDT, C50
    and T60 went through seed_finite_means, so a cohort whose loss or log_mse
    cohort the publication table refuses -- 6 212 finite queries of 6 217, or none
    at all -- still passed the pre-launch gate, through build_calibration and
    through the binder's calibration.measure route alike.
    
    seed_means now runs the table's own per-metric loop over every registered
    column with a non-null specification, bounding each one's finite cohort and
    seed means, and selects the three historical metrics only afterwards.  Native
    units are kept (no table scaling), and nothing here reads an approval pin.
    
