    exp_07 round 9: each product declares exactly its own dependencies
    
    Round-8 blocker 1: the hours ledger and the probe receipt were admissible but
    not required, although run_contract reads both unconditionally for every
    trained arm, so a product could omit six (table) or four (pairing) of them and
    still bind; and the upper bound was the arm's ENTIRE attempt declaration, so
    an unused epoch checkpoint, history.jsonl or the failed first attempt's
    abort.json passed as a dependency of a product that never read it.
    
    training_dependencies now returns everything a trained arm's contract consumes
    -- args.json, train_manifest.json, completion.json, the inventory sidecar, the
    hours ledger and the probe receipt -- and product_dependencies derives one
    EXACT map per product from its expected evaluations, those consumed inputs for
    the arms it used, the approval and its producer closure.  Declared must equal
    that map: an omission, an unknown input, a differing digest, a run the product
    did not use and an unused file of an arm it did use are each refused.  The
    complete attempt history stays bound in the report, as evidence, not as input;
    the attempt allowlist it fed is gone.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

